      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PEANUT BUTTER (5) gets the nod after a solid CL2 fourth at Kalgoorlie, where he was beaten a length and a half after sitting close and copping a bump at the start. His previous Kalgoorlie Mdn win over 1400m, achieved after racing wide throughout, gives the profile substance, and the weight relief is a genuine plus. LADY MONEY TALK (6) is the main danger fresh, having put together two CL1 thirds before the break and tuned up with a close Lark Hill trial. SMART ENERGY (3) has to answer for a well-beaten first-up run at this track, but his earlier Ascot CG Class 3 seventh as favourite was only beaten two and a half lengths, so a rebound keeps him in the placing mix. HANG GLIDER (4) resumes with two trials behind him, including a close second at Lark Hill, and his late-preparation Class 3 form was competitive enough to give him a minor hope if ready. JOTOPELI (7) won't be far away.",
